{
  "title": "Search debounce tasks in list/picker aren't cancelled on view \
dismiss",
  "description": "`Ramekin/RecipeListView.swift` and \
`Ramekin/RecipePickerSheet.swift` debounce search text by cancelling the \
previous `searchTask` before launching a new one. Neither cancels the \
outstanding task when the view disappears, so a search typed just before \
backing out still runs a list-recipes call (plus an unused `MainActor.run` \
state write on a vanished view). Add `.onDisappear { searchTask?.cancel() }` \
or store the task under a `@State` and let `.task { ... }` manage it.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
}
